 qgiv-embedjs')\; Have you ever been interested in joining Cool Petaluma's 
 block-based Cool Teams program but faced barriers to implementing it in yo
 ur neighborhood?&nbsp\; Thanks to the support of our two AmeriCorps fellow
 s\, Auggie and Raelyn\, Cool Petaluma will be offering a monthly Cool Team
 s program open to anyone interested in turning climate concern into collec
 tive action! Beginning on March 25th\, sessions will be held from 6 pm to 
 7:30 pm on the last Wednesday of each month. May’s session: Topic: Rethi
 nk Consumption: From food to fashion\, we can reimagine the full lifecycle
  of our stuff\, eliminating waste and pollution while increasing longevity
  and sharing. We’ll cover how to eat wisely\, shop smart and share more\
 , and vote with your dollar. Bring your own consumption hack ideas to shar
 e!&nbsp\; Location: Held at the brand new Porches office at 11 5th St (at 
 B st) For some entertaining and educational "Rethink Consumption" themed v
 ideos to&nbsp\;get you thinking about our next topic\, check out the Cool 
 Petaluma YouTube playlist here . (John Oliver’s Food Waste rant is a gre
 at one.) If you've been unable to implement our program in the past due to
  HOA&nbsp\;restrictions\, difficult neighborhood locations\, lack of time\
